<newsitem itemid="171538" id="root" date="1996-11-06" xml:lang="en">
<title>GERMANY: Hoechst details 9-month results.</title>
<headline>Hoechst details 9-month results.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to September 30</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit			5,663  vs  3,426</p>
<p>    Group sales				  38,408  vs 39,140</p>
<p>    Group foreign sales			31,463  vs 30,589</p>
<p>    Group domestic sales			6,945  vs  8,551</p>
<p>    Group operating profit		    4,067  vs  3,090</p>
<p>    Group net profit			    3,047  vs  1,918</p>
<p>Group net income after minority</p>
<p>    interests				    2,450   vs   1,469</p>
<p>    Group operating margin		   10.6    vs 7.9 pct</p>
<p>    Group personnel costs (excl pensions)9,517   vs  10,054</p>
<p>    Group workforce (average)	    151,993   vs 165,844</p>
<p>    Parent pre-tax profit		    1,846   vs  1,597</p>
<p>    Parent sales				 9,210   vs 10,991</p>
<p>    Parent domestic sales		    4,364   vs  5,094</p>
<p>    Parent foreign sales		     4,846   vs  5,897</p>
<p>    Parent personnel costs		   2,815   vs  3,181</p>
<p>    Parent workforce (average)	    36,399   vs 41,580</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts forecast only third quarter pre-tax profits excluding extraordinary earnings with estimates ranging between 802 million marks and 1.5 billion marks compared with last year's 3.426 billion mark level. Forecasts for sales ranged between 38.6 and 39.0 billion marks. Analysts said the predictions were difficult to make due to extraordinary factors.</p>
<p>Hoechst also said its personnel costs excluded retirement and pension costs.</p>
<p>Full name of German chemical company is Hoechst AG.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
